Phase 2 Development Plan (v1.3 & Beyond)
Overview
Phase 2 focuses on deferred refinements from v1.2, advanced reporting features, and scalability improvements. All items below are verified to NOT impact v1.2 core functionality and can proceed in parallel with testing.

PHASE 2A: Deferred PDF/UX Refinements
PDF-RFN-d: Per-Report PDF Export (Medium effort – 6–8 hours)
Scope: Separate PDF generation for Financial Statements, Auditor's Report, and Director's/Board's Report.

Deliverable: Three independent PDF files instead of combined export.

Implementation approach:

Refactor export_dialog.py: Add checkboxes for "Financial Statements PDF", "Auditor's Report PDF", "Director's/Board's Report PDF"
Update export handler to conditionally call:
_export_fs_pdf() → generates BS + P&L + CFS + Notes (existing logic, already compacted)
_export_auditor_pdf() → extracts Auditor's Report narrative text, renders via ReportLab Paragraph objects
_export_directors_pdf() → extracts Director's/Board's Report narrative, renders via ReportLab
File naming: {stem}_FS.pdf, {stem}_Auditors_Report.pdf, {stem}_Directors_Report.pdf
Narrative conversion: Extract template text from DOCX placeholders (e.g., {{AUDITOR_REPORT_TEXT}}), render as PDF with simple formatting (no tables, convert indents to spaces)
Testing: Verify three separate PDFs generated with correct naming, content separation, and file sizes reasonable (~200–500KB each).

Dependency: Requires Phase 2b (Narrative text extraction) to be functional first.

PDF-RFN-e: Narrative PDF Rendering (Medium effort – 4–6 hours)
Scope: Convert DOCX report narrative text to PDF with ReportLab.

Deliverable: Auditor's Report and Director's/Board's Report as formatted PDF pages (text-only, no embedded tables from DOCX).

Implementation approach:

Create finstruct/export/narrative_renderer.py:
Class NarrativeRenderer:
Method extract_text(docx_path: Path) -> dict — pulls text from DOCX placeholders
Method render_pdf(narrative_dict, output_path: Path, entity_type: str) — builds ReportLab Story with Paragraphs/Spacers
ReportLab styling: Use consistent fonts (Calibri 11pt body, 13pt headings), margins (20mm), header/footer with entity name and date
Support simple formatting: Bold, Italic, Underline (converted from DOCX runs)
Page breaks: Auto-inserted if narrative exceeds page height
Testing: Verify narrative PDFs open correctly, text readable, no corruption, page breaks sensible.

Dependency: None (independent module).

