Current ML API Implementation (Discovery Summary)
Where API is Integrated:
Files involved:

finstruct/data/settings_db.py — API key storage (encrypted)
finstruct/core/mapper.py — ledger-to-code prediction using Claude API
Current API Usage:
settings_db.py (Key Management):

Method get_api_key() — retrieves encrypted API key from settings
Method set_api_key(key) — stores encrypted API key
Encryption/decryption handled via Python cryptography library (Fernet symmetric encryption)
Key stored in settings table with key name "claude_api_key"
mapper.py (Prediction Logic):

Class LedgerMapper:
Initialization: api_key = self._sdb.get_api_key() (retrieves API key)
Method predict_code(ledger_name: str, group_hint: str = None) -> (code: str, confidence: float)
Uses Claude API to classify ledger names against known master_db codes
Confidence score indicates prediction accuracy (0.0–1.0 range)
Fallback: if API call fails or confidence < threshold (default 0.6), returns (None, 0.0) and prompts user for manual mapping
Workflow:
User imports TB → TB importer calls mapper.predict_code(ledger_name, group_hint)
Claude API receives prompt with ledger name + group hint + reference examples from master_db
API returns predicted code + confidence score
If confidence > threshold: auto-populate mapping; user can override
If confidence ≤ threshold: show as "?" in grid; user must select mapping manually
