ML Accuracy Performance Estimate
Observed Accuracy Levels (Inferred):
Exact matches (e.g., "Sales A/c" → "PL001"): ~95% confidence
Common variations (e.g., "Sales", "Revenue", "Total Sales"): ~75% confidence
Partial matches (e.g., "Sales & Service Income"): ~50% confidence
Suspense/temporary (e.g., "Suspense A/c", "Rounding"): ~15% confidence
Entity-specific (e.g., "Partner Capital" in non-LLP context): ~30% confidence
Overall accuracy (weighted): ~65–70% (estimated 65–70 out of 100 ledgers mapped correctly without user intervention)
Problem Areas:
False positives: Mapper may confidently mis-classify ledger (e.g., "Loan to Partners" classified as "Secured Loan" instead of "Long-Term Advances")
No group-aware logic: Mapper doesn't use group_hint to narrow search space
No typo tolerance: Misspelled names fail to match (e.g., "Salse A/c" instead of "Sales A/c")
No context from position: Doesn't consider whether ledger is Dr/Cr to disambiguate (e.g., "Interest" could be PL007 income or PL022 expense)
Recommendations for KB Enhancement (Phase 2E)
KB Expansion Strategy:
1. Extract Training Data from Real Projects (Quick Win – 1–2 hours)
Audit successful TB imports from user's existing projects (anonymize entity names)
Extract (ledger_name, group_hint, actual_code) tuples from successful imports
Filter for high-confidence matches only (confidence >0.8)
Build training dataset: ~100–200 verified examples
Effort: Low (automated extraction + manual review)
Payoff: Immediate 5–10% accuracy improvement
2. Systematic Coverage of NCE Entities (Medium effort – 3–4 hours)
Create example ledger sets for LLP, PROP, PART, AOP, TRUST covering all codes:

LLP: 60+ ledger examples covering Partner Capital, P&L revenue/expense variations, Partner Remuneration
PROP: 40+ examples (Proprietor-specific capital, drawings, P&L variations)
PART: 50+ examples (Partners' Capital, Partners' Loans, Appropriation accounts)
AOP: 45+ examples (Fund-based capital, I&E variations)
TRUST: 50+ examples (Corpus Fund, Earmarked Funds, Donations, FCRA-specific)
Format:

Ledger Name     | Group Hint      | Expected Code | Entity Type
Partners' Capital, Rajesh | Partner Capital | NP001 | LLP
Rajesh - Current A/c      | Partner Capital | NP001 | LLP
Partner Remuneration, Rajesh | P&L Expense  | NP003 | LLP
Maintenance Fund          | Capital Fund    | AO003 | AOP
Programme Expense - Education | Expenditure | AE010 | AOP
Corpus - Fixed Deposits   | Investment      | TR021 | TRUST
Effort: 3–4 hours (systematically enumerate all codes for each entity type + populate examples)

3. Typo Tolerance & Fuzzy Matching (Medium effort – 2–3 hours)
Enhance mapper.py to handle misspellings:

Use difflib.SequenceMatcher() or Levenshtein distance to find close matches
If exact match fails, try fuzzy match with similarity threshold (e.g., >0.8)
Example: "Salse A/c" (typo) → fuzzy match "Sales A/c" → code PL001 with confidence 0.85
Effort: 2–3 hours (implement fuzzy matching logic)

4. Group-Aware Code Prediction (Medium effort – 2–3 hours)
Refactor mapper to use group_hint to constrain code search:

Given group_hint (e.g., "Loans & Advances"), only consider codes tagged with that group (AS010–AS012 for company, NP004 for PART)
Weight predictions by group match: if group matches, confidence +15%
Example: "Partner Loan" + group_hint "Partner Capital" → boost confidence for NP004 (Partner Loans) over AS010 (Long-Term Advances)
Effort: 2–3 hours (refactor mapper.predict_code() logic)

5. Context-Aware Classification (Medium effort – 3–4 hours)
Use Dr/Cr balance information to disambiguate codes:

If ledger balance is always Cr (credit), narrow to codes that expect credit balances (e.g., income, liability, equity)
If balance is Dr (debit), narrow to codes that expect debit balances (e.g., expense, asset)
Example: "Interest" with Cr balance → likely PL007 (Interest Income), not PL022 (Finance Costs)
Integrate with WTB importer to pass balance_type hint to mapper
Effort: 3–4 hours (modify importer to pass hint; update mapper to use hint)

6. Language & Multilingual Support (Large effort – 6–8 hours, Deferred)
Add support for Hindi/regional ledger names:

Build KB with Hindi translations (e.g., "विक्रय खाता" → PL001)
Use language detection (e.g., langdetect library) to identify ledger language
Translate to English via Google Translate API (fallback) or pre-built Hindi-English ledger dictionary
Example: "विक्रय खाता" → translated to "Sales A/c" → mapped to PL001 with confidence 0.80
Effort: 6–8 hours (KB building, translation integration, testing across languages)
Deferred: Post-v1.2 (nice-to-have, not critical for English-language tool)

